Actually this is my first leetcode question in java script, So I got some learnings while doing this problem

Learnings:
1. JavaScript treats all numbers as floating-point decimals. If left = 0 and right = 3, then (0 + 3) / 2 results in 1.5. Trying to look up nums[1.5] yields undefined
2. for solving the above issue we use Math.floor() method to round of the floating value to the interger and rectify the js issue
3. As i am coding in c++ so i used double equal to sign, In javascript we use triple equal to sign for comparising
4. And we use Let keyword to initialise variables rather than traditional int as in c++

My code:-
/**
 * @param {number[]} nums
 * @param {number} target
 * @return {number}
 */
var search = function(nums, target) {
    let left  = 0 ; let right = nums.length-1;
    while(left<= right){
        let mid = Math.floor((left + right)/2);
        if(nums[mid]===target){
            return mid;
        }
        else if(target > nums[mid]){
            left = mid+1;
        }
        else{
            right = mid-1;
        }
    }
    return -1;
};
